<title>UK: U.K. Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</title>
<headline>U.K. Intervention Board details EU sugar sales.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A total 104,350 tonnes of current series white sugar received export rebates of a maximum 46.721 European Currency Units (Ecus) per 100 kilos at Wednesday's European Union (EU) tender, the U.K. Intervention Board said.</p>
<p>Out of this, traders in France received 41,500 tonnes, in Germany 21,000, in Belgium 18,850, in Denmark 14,000, in the UK 6,500 and in the Netherlands 2,500 tonnes, it added.</p>
</text>
